From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 22:31:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] Expose a test case's recorded choices as a reproduce blob

hegel_test_case_choices returns the base64 blob of the choices a live test
case has made so far, encoded exactly as a failure's reproduction blob, so
a frontend that generates whole values natively (and so never sees the
individual draws) can learn which choices the case made and replay it
through hegel_test_case_from_blob. Backed by a new `choices_blob` on the
backend trait, native-only, built from the case's nodes with the raw
prefix.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016mTrLpQ8SJg9RC9F1GH9Ac
